## 0. CURRENT STATE AUDIT

### What Exists Today

| Layer | Technology | State |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend | Next.js 16.1.6 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind 4, Recharts | Working, client-rendered pages |
| Backend | Next.js API Routes (serverless on Vercel) | Monolithic, all logic in route handlers |
| Database | PostgreSQL on Neon, Prisma 6.5 with `driverAdapters` | Single writer, no read replicas |
| Auth | NextAuth 5 beta, Google OAuth only | Session stored in DB |
| Trading Engine | Custom CLOB in `src/lib/clob.ts` | In-memory matching, DB persistence via `$transaction` |
| Deployment | Vercel (auto-deploy from `main`) | No staging environment |
| Caching | None | Every request hits DB |
| Monitoring | None | No observability, no alerting |
| Testing | None | Zero tests |
| Rate Limiting | None | APIs fully open |
| CI/CD | None | Push → auto-deploy |

### Critical Architecture Problems

1. **Trade execution is NOT concurrency-safe.** The `$transaction` in `/api/trade` reads resting orders, matches in JS, then writes fills. Two concurrent trades on the same market will read stale order books and produce incorrect fills. Prisma's interactive transactions use `SERIALIZABLE` isolation BUT Neon serverless driver doesn't guarantee this the same way — the timeout/retry behavior is undefined.

2. **No rate limiting anywhere.** A single user can fire 10,000 requests/second to `/api/trade` and exhaust Neon's connection pool.

3. **Leaderboard is an N+1 full table scan.** It fetches ALL users with ALL trades and ALL positions, computes in-memory, sorts, and returns top 50. At 10k users × 100 trades each, this query returns 1M+ rows.

4. **No input sanitization beyond basic null checks.** The trade route trusts `amount`, `price` as raw numbers. Floating-point edge cases (negative zero, NaN, Infinity) are not checked.

5. **User balance is a single `Float` field with no audit trail.** If any code path has a bug that increments/decrements incorrectly, the money evaporates with no way to reconstruct.

6. **Market maker bot runs as CLI only.** No cron automation, no monitoring of bot health.

7. **No market settlement system.** No API to resolve markets, no payout logic, no dispute mechanism.

8. **Session callback makes a DB query on EVERY request.** `auth()` in every route handler triggers the callback which queries `prisma.user.findUnique` for balance.

