### 1.7 Leaderboard Architecture Rewrite

Current: Fetches all users + all trades + all positions → computes in memory.

**New approach:** Materialized computation.

```prisma
model LeaderboardSnapshot {
  id              String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId          String
  totalProfit     Float
  positionValue   Float
  tradeCount      Int
  rank            Int
  computedAt      DateTime @default(now())
  user            User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])

  @@unique([userId, computedAt])
  @@index([computedAt, rank])
}
```

A Vercel Cron Job runs every 60 seconds:
1. Compute leaderboard for all active users (batch query)
2. INSERT snapshot rows
3. API reads latest snapshot (indexed, fast)

This turns an O(n × m) query into an O(50) read.

