## 4. SCALING TO 10,000 CONCURRENT USERS

### 4.1 Expected Bottlenecks

| Bottleneck | Why | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| Neon connection pool | Free tier = 20 connections. 10k users = instant exhaustion. | All requests fail with connection errors. |
| Trade transaction duration | Current avg ~200ms. Serial per market. | 5 trades/sec/market max. |
| Leaderboard query | Full table scan | 10+ second query, blocks connection pool. |
| Session auth callback | DB query per request | 10k requests = 10k queries for session alone. |
| Order book fetch | No caching | Same market page viewed by 1000 users = 1000 identical queries. |

### 4.2 Solutions

**Connection pool:** Upgrade Neon to Pro (300 pooled connections). Use `@neondatabase/serverless` with connection pooling URL:
```
DATABASE_URL=postgres://...@ep-xxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true
```

**Session caching:** Cache session data in Redis. After first auth() call, store user session in Redis with 5-minute TTL. Subsequent requests check Redis first.

```typescript
// auth.ts callback:
async session({ session, user }) {
  const cached = await redis.get(`session:${user.id}`);
  if (cached) return { ...session, user: cached };
  const dbUser = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { id: user.id }, select: { balance: true, role: true } });
  const userData = { ...session.user, id: user.id, balance: dbUser?.balance ?? 1000, role: dbUser?.role ?? "user" };
  await redis.set(`session:${user.id}`, userData, { ex: 300 });
  session.user = userData;
  return session;
}
```

**Invalidate on balance change:** After any trade/settlement, delete `session:{userId}` from Redis.

**Read replica:** Use Neon read replica for all GET endpoints. Write endpoints use primary.

```typescript
// lib/prisma.ts
export const prismaRead = new PrismaClient({
  datasources: { db: { url: process.env.DATABASE_URL_READ } },
});
```

**Static generation + ISR:** Home page markets list can use ISR with 10-second revalidation:
```typescript
// page.tsx
export const revalidate = 10;
```

